# Random modules like those of random-unique-1.test, whose value is the
# I/O state (generate-unique-programs.py --io), so that predicates of
# determinisms other than det, cc_multi and erroneous have I/O state
# arguments of an invalid determinism. merkc must report those, and its
# other errors, at the same lines as mmc.
#
# REQUIRES: mmc
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir %t
# RUN: %python %S/../../../utils/type-oracle/generate-unique-programs.py --io --seed 201 --count 40 %t
# RUN: %compare-switches --determinism %t/*.m
